# Pass the actual value explicitly as a process environment variable:
# sudo env HEADSCALE_HOSTNAME='your-existing-ngrok-hostname' \
#   bash headscale/rebuild.sh --check
# Use the same explicit environment with --install only when ready.
# --check reads host/package/port state and probes only unauthenticated local
# FastMCP 127.0.0.1:8765/mcp using the existing hostname as its Host header.
# Neither mode automatically changes or starts/stops the existing ngrok tunnel,
# FastMCP or Hysteria. --install starts only the new Headscale and local ingress.
#
# Prepared chain after a LATER manual ngrok switch:
# existing ngrok HTTPS -> 127.0.0.1:19080 Caddy -> Headscale 18080 / FastMCP 8765.
# TLS stays at ngrok, so no VPS IPv4 or ACME email parameter is used.
# Public DERP is enabled; embedded DERP and client DNS management are disabled.
# The ngrok special POST Upgrade path is still UNVERIFIED until real client QA.
